<header class="sp-head"><a class="sp-portrait" href="/encyclopedia/harold-macmillan" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/harold-macmillan.jpg" alt="" width="104" height="104"></a><p class="featured-region">3 February 1960 · Cape Town</p><h1 class="sp-title">Macmillan's Wind of Change</h1><p class="sp-by"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/harold-macmillan">Harold Macmillan</a></p></header>
<section class="sp-sec"><h2>The setting</h2><p>Early in 1960 the British prime minister Harold Macmillan toured Africa, visiting Ghana, Nigeria, the Federation of Rhodesia and Nyasaland and South Africa, as Britain prepared to give independence to more of its African colonies. He had first given the speech in Accra, where it drew little notice; on 3 February he gave it again to both houses of the Parliament of South Africa, then governed by Hendrik Verwoerd and his policy of apartheid.</p></section>
<section class="sp-sec"><h2>Key passage</h2><blockquote class="sp-quote"><p>The wind of change is blowing through this continent, and whether we like it or not, this growth of national consciousness is a political fact.</p></blockquote><p class="sp-source">Address to both houses of the Parliament of South Africa, Cape Town, 3 February 1960. Only this passage is quoted here.</p><div class="sp-full"><button type="button" class="sp-share" data-share-text="“The wind of change is blowing through this continent, and whether we like it or not, this growth of national consciousness is a political fact.” — Harold Macmillan, Macmillan's Wind of Change" data-share-img="/images/og/speech-macmillan-wind-of-change.jpg">Share this quote</button></div></section>
<section class="sp-sec"><h2>What followed</h2><p>The speech was received coldly in Cape Town. Britain's colonies in Africa became independent in quick succession, Tanganyika in 1961, Uganda in 1962 and Kenya in 1963, while South Africa voted to become a republic and left the Commonwealth in 1961.</p><div class="sp-led"><h3 class="sp-led-k">What it led to</h3><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/decolonisation">Decolonisation</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/commonwealth-of-nations">Commonwealth of Nations</a></div></div></section>
